annot(#noCore)

# A data value re-applied with a new parameter binding ([$F[$T -> $_B]], as core's [bindap] [fmap]
# arm declares its result): the fields the parameter governs follow the new binding. [Bx]'s [value]
# is declared [$T], so rebinding [T] on [Bx[$T -> X](value= X)] gives a [Bx] whose [value] is the
# new binding, not a [Bx] still holding an [X].
#noCore
module(Ad)
  data(X)
  data(Y)

  class(Opt[$T], [Bx[$T -> $_T](value -> $T), Nx])
